{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-168675-r4587233","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Tourte à la Lorraine","sourcePageId":168675,"sourceRevision":"4587233","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:28:37Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tourte%20%C3%A0%20la%20Lorraine&oldid=4587233","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:22.147Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:French recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for pastries","Category:Recipes for pot pie","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using heavy cream","Category:Recipes using pie dough","Category:Recipes using puff pastry","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"ae32edb8e3adf55130858c0334d64d984996d8a5ec073eea1e4584fea2c088a6","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Recipes for pastries\n| Yield = 1 tourte\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of France|French cuisine]]\n\n'''''Tourte à la Lorraine''''' is an elaborate meat pie with a [[Cookbook:Pâte brisée|''pâte brisée'']] (pie dough) base and a [[Cookbook:Puff pastry|puff pastry]] top which is baked. Ten minutes before the end of the baking period, a savoury egg-and-cream custard is poured through a hole in the pie crust and returned to the oven to set.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] [[Cookbook:Puff Pastry|puff pastry]]\n* 4 oz pie [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]]\n* 4 oz fresh [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] \n* 4 oz [[Cookbook:Veal|veal]], diced\n* 1 cup Riesling [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Shallot|shallots]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] cloves, [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaves]]\n* 2 sprigs [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n* 4-spice powder\n* [[Cookbook:Parsley|Parsley]], chopped\n* ½ cup heavy [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]]\n* 1 whole [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg Yolk|egg yolk]]\n* [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|Nutmeg]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine the meat, Riesling, salt, pepper, 4-spice powder, shallots, garlic, onion, parsley, bay leaves, thyme, and cloves.\n#[[Cookbook:Marinating|Marinate]] for 48 hours.\n#Preheat the [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 400°F.\n#Press the pie dough into a buttered and floured [[Cookbook:Pie and Tart Pans|pie dish]] or cake pan lined with [[Cookbook:Parchment Paper|parchment paper]].\n#Place the meat on the pie dough leaving a narrow border all around the edge. Cover the meat with the puff pastry, taking care to moisten with a little water to glue the edges together.\n#[[Cookbook:Brush|Brush]] the surface with egg yolk and make a small chimney in the middle (you may use a tube of cardboard covered with foil). Make a pleasing design on the surface of the pastry with a tip of a small knife.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] in a hot [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] for 45 minutes.\n#During this time, [[Cookbook:Beating|beat]] the egg and yolk with the cream. Season with grated nutmeg, salt and pepper.\n#Remove the pie from the oven and, with the help of a funnel, pour the cream mixture through the chimney. This operation is a bit delicate. One needs to add a little at a time and then tilt the pan to disperse the liquid throughout the pie.\n#Return to the oven for 10 minutes.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for pot pie]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:French recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for pastries]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using heavy cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using puff pastry]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pie dough]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Tourte à la Lorraine","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 oz puff pastry","sourceText":"4 oz puff pastry","amountText":"4 oz puff pastry","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 oz pie dough","sourceText":"4 oz pie dough","amountText":"4 oz pie dough","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"4 oz fresh pork, diced","sourceText":"4 oz fresh pork, diced","amountText":"4 oz fresh pork, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"4 oz veal, diced","sourceText":"4 oz veal, diced","amountText":"4 oz veal, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 cup Riesling wine","sourceText":"1 cup Riesling wine","amountText":"1 cup Riesling wine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"2 shallots, chopped","sourceText":"2 shallots, chopped","amountText":"2 shallots, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 onion","sourceText":"1 onion","amountText":"1 onion","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 garlic cloves, minced","sourceText":"2 garlic cloves, minced","amountText":"2 garlic clov